/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-30T09:21:56Z","updated_at":"2026-08-30T09:21:56Z","body":"This is a bit of a rabbit hole 😓 The root cause is way older and pretty complex. Even before 4.7.2 this MRP does have wrong behavior when deleting that line. After deleting the line, the error about the line is still being reported:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/23deabd0-545a-4c7e-9781-e7094f4ea6bb\n\nThe issue here is that the analyzer tries to get an external parser for the script it is currently analyzing. This leads to retrieving an outdated parser from the cache and producing outdated errors. Previously we could just display the outdated position for those errors, now the script editor has to format the position to be human readable which fails, because the old error position is out of bounds in the new script content.\n\nI'd suggest we do a defensive programming fix for this to quickly address the crash. We should open a separate issue about the outdated errors issue.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5467861260/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]